✅ What is GitHub?

GitHub is a cloud-based platform for hosting code, managing projects, and collaborating using Git version control.

💡 Simple Explanation:

“GitHub is like Google Drive for code — it stores code online and tracks changes using Git.”

✅ Why GitHub is used?

To store/code repositories online
To track all changes and version history
To collaborate with team members
To handle branching, merging, PRs
For CI/CD, deployments, documentation
To show projects to recruiters (portfolio)

“GitHub is a code hosting platform that uses Git. I used it for version control, storing my projects, maintaining branches, and tracking every update. 
It helps me collaborate and keep a clean development workflow.”

✅ What is VS Code?

VS Code is a lightweight and powerful code editor created by Microsoft.

✅ Why VS Code is used?

Fast and lightweight
Tons of extensions (ESLint, Prettier, React, Tailwind, Docker etc.)
Integrated terminal, debugger
Git integration built-in
Very customizable

✅ How YOU used VS Code

Say this:
“I used VS Code for writing all my frontend and backend code. I also used extensions like ESLint, Prettier, and 
Tailwind CSS IntelliSense, and used the integrated terminal for running servers and Git commands.”

✅ What is Postman?
Postman is an API testing platform used to send HTTP requests and test backend APIs.

✅ Why Postman is used?

Test GET, POST, PUT, DELETE APIs
Send headers, cookies, tokens (JWT)
Test authentication logic
Debug server issues
Check responses before connecting frontend
Create API collections for teams

✅ How YOU used Postman

Your interview explanation:

“In my project, I used Postman to test all backend REST APIs like login, register, products, and payments. I tested request bodies, 
authentication using JWT tokens, and error handling. It helped me verify API performance before connecting it to the frontend.”


